The reflection $(x,n)\mapsto(-x,n)$ preserves $\widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^{2}_{+}$ together with its oriented
graph structure and, because the opening probability $p_{\xi_{n}}$ depends only
on the height~$n$, it preserves the law $\mathbb{P}^{\xi}$ for every environment
$\xi$. Since it exchanges $H_{0}^{-}$ and $H_{0}^{+}$, the processes $(\ell_{n})_{n\ge0}$ and $(-r_{n})_{n\ge0}$ have the same law, and it suffices to treat the right edge.

By Lemma~\ref{lem:basic} below, whose proof does not rely on this section, the
set $\zeta_{m}(H_{0}^{-})$ is almost surely non-empty, so that $r_{m}>-\infty$
almost surely. For $0\le m\le n$ let $X_{m,n}:=\max\zeta_{m,n}\bigl(H_{m}^{r_{m}}\bigr)-r_{m}$.

