Let $\widehat{\mathcal{F}}_{m}:=\sigma\bigl((\xi_{i})_{i\ne m},\,(U_{z})_{z\in\widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^{2}_{+},\,z_{2}\le m}\bigr),$ and let $G_{m}$ and $B_{m}$ be the sets $\zeta_{m}(H_{0}^{-})$
computed under $\xi^{m,G}$ and $\xi^{m,B}$ respectively. The two environments
differ only on $H_{m}$, so the occupation variables are the same at every height
but $m$. In particular, $r_{m-1}$ is identical for both.

Let $v:=(r_{m-1}+1,m)$. On $\{p_{c}\le U_{v}<p_{G}\}$ the site $v$ is open under
$\xi^{m,G}$ and closed under $\xi^{m,B}$. Thus, on this event $\max G_{m}\ge r_{m-1}+1$ and $\max B_{m}\le r_{m-1}-1$, so $\max G_{m}> \max B_{m}$.
Conditionally on $\mathcal{F}_{m-1}$ the site $v$ is deterministic, and $U_{v}$
is at height $m$, so it is independent of $\mathcal{F}_{m-1}$. Thus,
$\mathbb{P}(p_{c}\le U_{v}<p_{G}\mid\mathcal{F}_{m-1})=p_{G}-p_{c}$ almost surely, and

